@options
@opt **--config** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --config <path>
@cli help: Read a schema-1 configuration

Read exactly one schema-1 JSON configuration. Its role must match the
program: client for **yume**, server for **yumed**. Required unless
**--help** or **--version** is requested. Security policy has no
command-line overrides.
@opt **--validate**
@cli spell: --validate
@cli help: Check local configuration and credentials, then exit

Check schema, role, referenced credentials, direct-adapter destination
policy and the daemon's module programs, then exit without opening a listener
or network connection. This
checks local inputs; it does not test connectivity or complete runtime startup,
including loading the cover site, matching services to runtime adapters,
TUN privileges or DNS authorization.
@opt **--version**
@cli spell: --version
@cli help: Print local versions and provider information

Print the product version, transport version, configuration schema, suite,
session-security provider, crypto backend and evidence profile. This operation
uses local information and does not read a configuration or contact a server.
@opt **--completion** *shell*
@cli values: bash
@cli spell: --completion <shell>
@cli help: Print the shell completion script and exit

Print the completion script for *shell*, which must be **bash**, and exit.
The script completes this program's options, their fixed values and file
arguments. To load it for one user, save it under the program's name in
*~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/*. This operation reads no
configuration.
@opt **-h, --help**
@cli spell: -h, --help
@cli help: Print this help and exit

Print the supported options and exit. Unknown arguments still fail parsing
when combined with **--help**, **--version** or **--completion**.
@end
